---
/**
 * terms.astro — terms of use (D-280).
 *
 * What it is: terms sized to what this site actually does today — a
 * pre-launch marketing page with a beta-signup form, no purchase, no
 * account, no live product download. Written to match that reality rather
 * than a generic SaaS terms template with clauses for things (subscriptions,
 * user content, refunds) that do not exist here.
 * What it does NOT do: name a governing law or jurisdiction — that is a real
 * decision only the owner can make (where the business is actually
 * domiciled), left as an explicit placeholder rather than guessed. See the
 * note at the bottom and D-280 in the decision log.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';

const updated = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — Apelles"
  description="The terms for using the Apelles website and its pre-launch beta signup. Short version: the software is AGPL-3.0, there is no product to buy yet, and the beta signup is a request, not a guarantee."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms"
    lede={`Last updated ${updated}. This site is a pre-launch marketing page. There is no purchase, no account, and no live product download here yet — these terms are sized to that.`}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        This is the marketing and pre-launch site for Apelles, a video editor built on top of a
        vendored fork of <a class="link" href="https://github.com/CyberTimon/RapidRAW">RapidRAW</a>.
        There is no application to download from this site yet — the only thing it does is describe
        the product and let you leave an email address to hear about it when there is a build worth
        installing.
      </p>

      <h2>The beta signup is a request, not a guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        Submitting the form means you have asked to be told when a beta build exists. It does not
        reserve you a place in any program, does not create an account, and does not obligate us to
        contact you by any date or at all if the project changes direction. See the
        <a class="link" href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for exactly what happens to the address
        you give us.
      </p>

      <h2>The software's own licence</h2>
      <p>
        Apelles itself — the application, once it exists as a build — is free software under the
        <span class="mono">AGPL-3.0</span> licence, the same licence its vendored engine
        (RapidRAW) ships under. These website terms govern this site; they do not modify or
        override the AGPL-3.0 licence that governs the software itself. Read the licence directly
        at <a class="link" href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html">gnu.org</a> for what it
        actually permits and requires.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty, pre-release</h2>
      <p>
        Everything on this site describes software that is pre-release. Where the AGPL-3.0 licence
        already disclaims warranty for the software itself, that disclaimer stands; separately, the
        content of this website (the copy, the claims about what is shipped) is provided as
        accurately as we can make it at the time of writing, but the project is actively changing
        and a claim here can become stale before this page is next updated.
      </p>

      <h2>What you can do with this site's own content</h2>
      <p>
        The words and design of this website are not open-source in the way the application is —
        please don't reproduce this site's own copy or design elsewhere as though it were yours.
        The application's own source code is separately licensed under AGPL-3.0 as described above,
        and that licence, not these terms, governs your rights to that code.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change, this page changes in the same commit as whatever prompted it — that
        is a standing rule for this whole codebase (see this repo's own
        <code class="mono">CLAUDE.md</code>), not a promise made separately from the code.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: email
        <a class="link" href="mailto:ashish.1999vns@gmail.com">ashish.1999vns@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="fine">
        <strong>Governing law is deliberately left blank here.</strong> A real terms-of-use document
        names the jurisdiction and law that governs it, which depends on where the business behind
        this site is actually domiciled — a fact this page cannot invent. Fill that in (and have the
        whole page reviewed by a lawyer) before relying on it for a real public launch; this page is
        a good-faith draft sized to what the site currently does, not a substitute for legal advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose .link {
    color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--pigment-terracotta) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .prose .link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
  }

  .fine {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
  }
</style>
